 <46025606+Ken5998@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:28:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] perf: let the CPU prepare the next frame while the GPU
 draws

On Wayland, pre_present_notify makes winit hold the next RedrawRequested
until the compositor's frame callback, which arrives only once the GPU has
finished the frame and it was shown. CPU and GPU then never overlap: on a
GPU-bound handheld a frame costs CPU time + GPU time. Leave it out (the
swapchain paces the frames); MCLA_PRESENT_NOTIFY=1 restores it.
---
 mcla-rs/crates/game/src/main.rs | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mcla-rs/crates/game/src/main.rs b/mcla-rs/crates/game/src/main.rs
index b1c6ab2..93003a1 100644
--- a/mcla-rs/crates/game/src/main.rs
+++ b/mcla-rs/crates/game/src/main.rs
@@ -10915,7 +10915,14 @@ log::info!("stuck2: car {} {} grounded {} up.y {:.2} speed {:.2} rpm {:.0} veh {
         let t_enc = now.elapsed().as_secs_f32() * 1000.0;
         gpu.queue.submit(early_cbs.into_iter().chain([enc.finish()]));
         gpuprof::after_submit();
-        window.pre_present_notify();
+        // (On Wayland this makes winit hold the next RedrawRequested until the compositor's frame
+        // callback, which comes only once the GPU has finished this frame and the compositor has
+        // shown it: the CPU then never prepares a frame while the GPU draws the last one. On a
+        // GPU-bound handheld that is CPU time + GPU time a frame instead of the larger of the
+        // two, so it is left out; the swapchain paces the frames. MCLA_PRESENT_NOTIFY=1: as upstream.)
+        if std::env::var("MCLA_PRESENT_NOTIFY").map_or(false, |v| v.trim() == "1") {
+            window.pre_present_notify();
+        }
         frame.present();
         let t_end = now.elapsed().as_secs_f32() * 1000.0;
         if self.framelog.is_some() {
